34,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"My findings are a bit worrying. It seems projects based on ""appeal"" often slip by a year, and we lose many weeks to rain and frost on outdoor work.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh! I found out that general-purpose rooms are always full, while specialist ones are mostly empty. Also, taking rooms out of service costs us a lot in off-site rentals!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"It is as I feared. We have unfilled grounds posts, but our technicians are wasting hours on manual checks because the old equipment can't do it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My data shows that shared, bookable spaces are rated highest by users. However, the older blocks are risky; hazardous materials have caused huge delays recently.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"As expected, the market is unkind. Mechanical and ducting costs have jumped by a fifth, and we have no reserve to replace old audiovisual kit.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Yumi, the cost of off-site rentals is quite a burden. We must be very careful not to squeeze a year of work into a few weeks at the end.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, I agree! And @Mizuki, if shared spaces are the most popular, maybe we should look for a project that creates more of those?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Benjamin, if mechanical costs are rising, we should be cautious. But we also cannot ignore the technicians who are struggling with manual routines.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that is true, but if we pick a project in an older block, the hazardous materials will just create more delays and stress for everyone.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, a fascinating point. We are caught between the need for utility and the reality of decaying infrastructure and rising costs.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we must avoid outdoor work due to the weather and avoid ""appeal"" projects that slip. We need something necessary and predictable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,And something that doesn't take too many rooms out of service! I don't want us to spend the whole budget on off-site rentals.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"I still believe the priority should be relieving the staff. If the equipment is failing and requiring manual work, that is a systemic failure.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree with George on the need for relief, but only if the project is a ""necessary"" one that won't slip and doesn't hit hazardous materials.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,I find it charming that we are all discovering the same tragedy. We are planning for a world that no longer exists financially or operationally.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
