60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Looking at the candidates, the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade seems the most sensible. It is a necessary upgrade, not just for ""appeal,"" so it should stay on schedule.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I like the Central Study Commons because it creates shared space, but @Mizuki, is that in an older block? I'm worried about the rentals and the hazards.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,The Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade is the only one that helps my technicians. It replaces the equipment that forces them into those manual routines.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, the Study Commons is in a ground-floor hall, which is exactly where the hazardous materials are. The Ventilation Upgrade is a better, more necessary choice.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The Path Network is too exposed to the weather, and the Media Center's AV kit would have no renewal fund. The Ventilation Upgrade is the most grounded.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"I agree. The Ventilation Upgrade avoids the weather risks of the paths and the scheduling slips of ""appeal"" projects like the Media Center.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"If the Study Commons is too risky because of the hazards, then I'm on board with the Ventilation Upgrade. It's better to be safe!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,It is the only choice that addresses the staffing strain. I am quite stubborn about this; we cannot ignore the people doing the work.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"It aligns with the data. It's a necessary infrastructure project, which means it's less likely to disappoint the users or slip in timing.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While the mechanical costs are rising, the lack of an alternative that doesn't invite disaster makes the Ventilation Upgrade the only logical path.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I feel a great sense of peace that we have found a solution that protects both the schedule and the staff.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"Me too! It's not as ""flashy"" as a media center, but it's the right thing to do for the campus.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,I am satisfied. It is a practical decision that provides real relief to the technicians.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I concur. It is the most rational choice based on the post-occupancy and survey data.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare moment of total alignment. I shall join this chorus of pragmatism.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I vote for the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I vote for the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade!,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,I vote for the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,I vote for the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
